SOUNDDVR.DVR sound-source REGISTER (asm 0x1ec / 0xaf4): read the engine-published AX/BX/ES and rebase
the descriptor copy to the driver's own data segment.

The register method is reached via the engine be0e (patch 349) through DGROUP:0x510 -> 01ec -> 0af4.
The __allregs indirect-vector dispatch dropped the register args, so:
  * 01ec's `param_1 != -1` gate (asm 0x1ec: `cmp ax,0xffff`) ran on garbage AX -> read g_snd_reg_ax.
  * 0af4 (asm 0xaf4) copies a 0x20-byte sound descriptor from ES:BX into the driver struct with ES =
    the descriptor SEGMENT (a dropped `unaff_ES`), BX the offset (0), AX the sound value.  Additionally
    every `ds:` access is to the DRIVER data segment (cs:[0x831]<<4 = load_seg+0x2a5), which Ghidra
    rendered as a mix of engine-DGROUP DAT_1000_cNN and host-absolute derefs.

Asm 0xaf4 (verified vs re_out/fist_snd_image.bin):
    af4: mov ds, cs:[0x831]          ; DS = driver data seg
    af9: test al,1; je 0xb10
    afd: cmpw [ds:0xe],0; je 0xb10
    b04: mov [ds:0x4],ax; mov [ds:0x0],es; mov [ds:0x2],bx; ret     ; (queued path)
    b10: mov [ds:0xa],ax; mov [ds:0x8],bx; mov [ds:0x6],es
    b1b: si=bx+0x10
    b26: rep: al=es:[si]; [ds:bx+0x20]=al   (0x10 bytes)
    b34: rep: al=es:[si]; [ds:bx+0x2a]=al; [ds:bx+0x34]=0xff  (0x10 bytes)
    b49: [ds:0xc]=si
    b4d: call 0xc94(ax)              ; ax.lo = last byte read
    b50: [ds:0x14]=1 ; [ds:0xe]=0xffff

Reached only under FIST_SB (c510 is populated only by the FIST_SB-gated 014e section install); the
default boot never enters here -> the 26 video flows stay byte-identical.
